Cell G2 sits at Q=1 (F2) under the 2019 header (G1), so it should return the maximum 2019 price for that quarter. The manual MAX formulas in column C already compute these per-quarter maximums; G2 needs a version that fills across years and down quarters.

For Q1 2019, the date window is from DATE(G$1,($F2-1)*3+1,1) up to, but not including, the first day of the next quarter, DATE(G$1,$F2*3+1,1). If quarter 4 gives month 13, DATE rolls it into January of the next year, so that case still works.

{"formula": "=MAXIFS($B$2:$B$45,$A$2:$A$45,\">=\"&DATE(G$1,($F2-1)*3+1,1),$A$2:$A$45,\"<\"&DATE(G$1,$F2*3+1,1))"}

