Column J ("month payed") should show which pay month each completed date in column I falls into. Each pay period starts on the "In (from)" date in column B, and those dates are sorted ascending. `LOOKUP` therefore finds the last start date on or before I3 and returns the matching "Month of pay" from column A. For example, 2011-11-11 falls after 2011-10-23, so it returns 2011-11-01.

I didn't use the "Out (too)" dates in column C because several of them have the wrong year. The `IF(I3="","",...)` part leaves the cell blank when there is no completed date.

{"formula": "=IF(I3=\"\",\"\",LOOKUP(I3,$B$3:$B$41,$A$3:$A$41))"}

H6 sits on the "Total Vacation Days (since start date)" row. G10 computes `=H6-G8`, which subtracts only the 2017 days taken. So H6 most likely starts from the carried-over 2016 balance in H5.

This is a best guess. If the user also adds a 2017 accrual (similar to the sick-hours calculation in Q6), the rate isn't shown in the sheet, so I've left it out.

{"formula": "=H5"}

