{"formula": "=LINEST(B12:K12,B11:K11^{1;2;3;4})"}

Q16 sits under the "A" header, so I read it as fund A's monthly allocation. This is a low-confidence guess. It spreads fund A's total grant ($D$3) over the months in proportion to the "Days (A:D)" count in column O. Column O is still empty, so this only works once O16:O40 is filled in.

